#BAGG
# Two players, two types each, no function nodes.  Player 1's types have action sets
# {0, 1} and {1, 2}, which share action node 1; player 2's types have {3, 4} and {4, 5},
# sharing node 4.  A player's payoff depends only on the opponent's chosen action node:
#
#   player 1 payoff (rows: own node 0, 1, 2; columns: opponent node 3, 4, 5)
#       4 0 2
#       1 3 0
#       0 2 5
#   player 2 payoff (rows: own node 3, 4, 5; columns: opponent node 0, 1, 2)
#       1 3 2
#       2 0 1
#       0 1 4
#
# Type priors are exact and unequal: player 1 (1/3, 2/3); player 2 (1/4, 3/4).
